inting ... would then carry the same value with no further change'","gate_dispatch.py:174 `gate_config(with_identity(cfg, ctx.ticket_id, \"review-plan\"))` — with_identity is an argument, evaluated before the with-body enters","gate_dispatch.py:706 `with gate_config(with_identity(cfg, ticket_id, \"verify-completion\")), collect_step_failures():`","run_identity.py:69 mint_run_identity reads _recording_span_trace_id() at call time"],"finding":"The plan's edit scope for gate_dispatch.py omits the ordering constraint that the run span must be entered BEFORE with_identity runs; as written, with_identity(cfg, ...) is evaluated as an argument to gate_config(...) (lines 174 and 706), which executes mint_run_identity before the with-body opens, so a run span opened inside/alongside that same with block would not yet be the active recording span and mint_run_identity would still mint rather than read it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5de7479bcbe78bdd","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope + Approach; src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:174, :706","norm_id":"ndc5a250a810b3b56","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A plan-review run where the run span is opened in the same with-statement as gate_config: mint_run_identity runs first and mints a fresh id, so the header and the run span diverge — the exact defect the ticket sets out to fix"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Enter the run span as an outer context (or explicitly before) the gate_config(with_identity(...)) call, so the recording span is active when with_identity runs at both boundaries.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State whether the code-review gate run (produce_code_review_verdict) is in or out of scope for the run span, and if out, give the positive reason it is excluded despite having the same candidate-span fan-out.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Approach: 'Open one rebar-owned span at each gate run boundary (workflow/gate_dispatch.py's two gate_config sites)'","gate_dispatch.py defines a THIRD gate run, produce_code_review_verdict, that runs gates/code-review.yaml with a CodeReviewBatchRunner fan-out and reuses candidate_span via wrap_candidate — its candidate spans are separate trace roots too","The epic's rationale for excluding review-code ('opens no gate scope', no with_identity) concerns header CORRELATION, not the candidate-span tracing fragmentation this plan fixes"],"finding":"The plan scopes the run span to only the two gate_config sites (plan-review, completion), but produce_code_review_verdict is a third gate-run boundary with its own multi-pass batch fan-out whose per-candidate spans are equally separate trace roots; the plan neither includes it nor justifies excluding it, so code-review remains many-traces-per-run — the exact defect the plan's title ('per gate run') claims to fix.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f85a7af3fef2407e4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope; gate_dispatch.py:492-600 (_run_code_review_gate)","norm_id":"ne184965592405906","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An operator runs `rebar review-code` through a gateway with tracing enabled and sees many Langfuse traces for one code-review run, identical to the plan-review defect this plan resolves"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a scope sentence: either extend the run span to the code-review boundary (noting it has no with_identity/gate_config, so the span alone — not correlation — is the benefit), or explicitly defer it with a reason.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make explicit that the run span must open and become the current span BEFORE the with_identity(...) call at each site, so mint_run_identity reads the run span's trace id rather than minting.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["run_identity.py:61-69 mint_run_identity reads _recording_span_trace_id() (the ACTIVE span) at call time","gate_dispatch.py:174 `gate_config(with_identity(cfg, ctx.ticket_id, \"review-plan\"))` — with_identity is evaluated when the with-statement's context-manager arguments are built","Plan says the span is opened 'at each gate run boundary ... so every agent call in the run nests beneath it' but does not state it must enclose the with_identity call specifically"],"finding":"The correlation acceptance criterion depends on the run span being the current OTel span at the moment mint_run_identity runs, but with_identity is evaluated inline as the gate_config(...) argument; the plan does not make explicit that the run span must open BEFORE (enclose) that with-statement line, which is the load-bearing ordering fact for the correlation to hold.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"faae92a635c78f833","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach; Acceptance Criteria (correlation AC); gate_dispatch.py:174, :706","norm_id":"nca1740005182aa27","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer opens the run span INSIDE the existing `with (...)` block (after with_identity has already minted), so mint_run_identity sees no recording span and mints a fresh id — the header and exported spans diverge and the correlation AC fails despite the span existing"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile the run-span patch-site inventory with all gate-run boundaries in gate_dispatch.py: either add produce_code_review_verdict / _run_code_review_gate (line 530) as a third run-span site, or state a positive reason it is out of scope given it also emits per-candidate spans via wrap_candidate.","cohort":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"criteria":["project.symbol-reference-completeness"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Open one rebar-owned span at each gate run boundary (`workflow/gate_dispatch.py`'s two `gate_config` sites), so every agent call in the run nests beneath it and the run is one trace.'","gate_dispatch.py has three gate-run boundaries: gate_config(with_identity(...)) at line 174 (produce_plan_review_verdict) and line 706 (produce_completion_verdict), PLUS _run_code_review_gate at line 530 (produce_code_review_verdict) which runs _ex.run_workflow with RunnerAgentStep/CodeReviewBatchRunner but no gate_config/with_identity.","Candidate spans are attached at model_classes.py:477 via wrap_candidate, which the code-review runner path also drives — so the code-review gate emits the same per-candidate spans the plan wants nested."],"finding":"The plan's run-span patch-site inventory ('workflow/gate_dispatch.py's two gate_config sites') omits a third gate-run boundary in the SAME file: _run_code_review_gate (line 530), called from produce_code_review_verdict. That path runs a full agent workflow (RunnerAgentStep + CodeReviewBatchRunner) and therefore emits per-candidate spans via wrap_candidate (model_classes.py:477), so it is a genuine gate run whose candidate spans stay separate trace roots — the exact many-traces defect the plan sets out to fix. Because the code-review gate uses gate_source.gate_read_root rather than gate_config(with_identity(...)), an inventory keyed on 'gate_config sites' silently excludes it, and the plan gives no positive rationale for the exclusion.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f90e11429b4bf73a3","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — 'Open one rebar-owned span at each gate run boundary (workflow/gate_dispatch.py's two gate_config sites)'","norm_id":"n8318d917cbbf853f","priority":0.9,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["produce_code_review_verdict / _run_code_review_gate (gate_dispatch.py:530): a code-review run's per-candidate spans remain independent trace roots, so a code-review still appears in Langfuse as many traces — the defect the plan claims to close for gate runs is left open for one of the three gate surfaces.","The plan's stated Scope edit ('open and close the run span at both boundaries') under-delivers: the code-review boundary gets no run span, and (lacking with_identity) no correlated header either."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Amend Scope to enumerate the run-span sites by derivation from the gate-run boundaries in gate_dispatch.py (produce_plan_review_verdict, produce_completion_verdict, produce_code_review_verdict), not by 'gate_config sites'; if code-review is intentionally excluded, record why (e.g. it opens no gate_config/with_identity scope) and note the consequence for its candidate-span traces.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify that the run span is opened/closed via a context manager (try/finally) so it closes and records the error even when a gate run raises, and add an AC exercising the raise-in-run path.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'open and close the run span at both boundaries' — no mention of context-manager/try-finally semantics on the error path","No AC exercises a gate run that raises while the span is open"],"finding":"The plan opens and closes a run span but does not specify that the span is closed on exception paths (e.g. a candidate call raises mid-run), risking a leaked/unexported span or a swallowed error.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fefe513aac4981a01","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: gate_dispatch.py 'open and close the run span at both boundaries'","norm_id":"naf30140341105848","priority":0.625,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A candidate call or verify step raises during a gate run; the run span must still close and record the error rather than leak"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Wrap the run at each gate_config site in a `with run_span(...)` that closes on exception; add an edge AC asserting the span still closes (and the error is surfaced, not swallowed) when a candidate call raises.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State that the run span is closed on the exception path (e.g. opened as a context manager / try-finally) so a mid-run failure cannot leak an open span and mis-parent later runs.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["T9"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.325,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan says 'open and close the run span at both boundaries' but names no exception path.","Candidate spans nest via contextvar (copy_context); an unclosed run span on an exception could remain the active parent for later work in the same context."],"finding":"The run span lifecycle defines CREATE (open at boundary) and normal RETIRE (close at boundary) but does not state that the span is closed when the gate run raises mid-way, risking a leaked/never-ended span that corrupts trace parentage for subsequent runs sharing the contextvar.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbd03f51e4b89882a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / gate_dispatch.py — 'open and close the run span at both boundaries'","norm_id":"n996be08a1c793a7b","priority":0.625,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A gate run that raises inside a candidate call leaves the run span open; a following run's spans nest under the stale span, producing a wrong/merged trace."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Open the run span as a context manager wrapping both gate_config sites so normal and exceptional exits both end the span.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the run span's name and any attributes (e.g. gate/run identifiers) in the plan so the factory contract is not left to the executor.",